+# T15 checkpoint documentation draft — source verified, qualification pending
+
+Prepared 2026-11-02 against HEAD `75bc8e438caaf4eadf8f4e0f6b522f84c680c1e7`; current root-frozen global candidate tree `f71c52fad680a74da1b90cc7470455fc90f4fa3f`. The five implementation sources below retain their exact reviewed hashes; the global tree also includes other bounded owners' repairs. Earlier review/runtime artifacts retain their original candidate identities. This ignored draft is ready for root's documentation reconciliation after the actual fullR2/native results. It is not a qualification receipt or an implementation plan. No tracked documentation was changed.
+
+## Candidate behavior and purpose
+
+T15 connects population learning to recorded successor legality for flat uniform/PER and recurrent uniform/PER learners. Both vanilla and Double DQN use the recorded mask of the exact replay successor. Vanilla selects the largest legal target value; Double selects with legal online values and evaluates that action with the target network. With gamma zero the target helper returns finite canonical rewards without reading Q entries for successor selection; tensor metadata validation and population network forwards still run. Non-bootstrap successor values are exactly zero. On bootstrapped rows every legal selector Q entry and the chosen target Q entry must be finite; nonfinite illegal or unused terminal outputs do not enter target arithmetic. Real rewards and final targets must be finite. This removes live-world legality from historical Bellman targets. Sources: [target implementation](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/training/q_targets.py:19), [flat and recurrent consumption](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:675).
+
+Replay admission captures actual successor masks alongside canonical DAC total and component rewards. Only predecessor lanes active on entry enter replay; flat admission chunks eligible rows at the actual capacity without changing their order. Recurrent collection retains exact successor observations, masks and recorded bits until the existing terminal/explicit-flush commit. Pending collector rows do not become retained replay merely because they exist. Sources: [episode commit](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:927), [production admission and clocks](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:1303).
+
+An update requires a scheduled opportunity, the retained eligible-transition warmup, and backend sampleability for the selected law and window policy. Warmup and batch size are independent authoring parameters: authored `min_size` is positive and no greater than capacity, while the obsolete `batch_size <= min_size` restriction is removed. The explicit construction seam accepts a nonnegative retained-transition threshold. Flat uniform/successive PER need B sampleable rows; replacement PER needs positive support and may draw B greater than the population. Recurrent warmup counts retained transitions, while B counts sampleable windows/contexts. Successive recurrent PER needs B distinct units; replacement PER and accepted uniform sequence adapters may draw B from fewer positive-support units. Fixed-full windows must actually exist; adaptive prefixes contain only real rows. The population requests readiness before drawing and logs changed unready reason/retained/sampleable diagnostics. Sources: [schema](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/config/training_v2_config.py:102), [request translation](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:654), [readiness gate](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:715); backend cardinality details are attributed source-verified prose in [sequence API handoff](/workspace/hamlet/.superpowers/sdd/2026-11-01-bac-remediation-upgrades/wave09-preparation/T15-sequence-serialization-api.md:9), whose implementation links were not followed.
+
+Recurrent learning groups sampled units by their real length, starts each online and target prefix with separate zero hidden state, and carries each network's own hidden state through real current observations. The online current-prefix state stays graph-connected across the complete sampled horizon for BPTT. Target-prefix advancement and all online/target bootstrap evaluations run under no-grad. Each bootstrap branches from the after-current prefix to that row's exact stored successor; the online branch also receives detached hidden tensors, and every bootstrap-returned hidden state is discarded. Padding never enters network evaluation, target construction or residual arithmetic. Double DQN adds an online successor branch at every real timestep in each length group, rather than one boundary forward per update. Source: [exact recurrent evaluation](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:675).
+
+The recurrent objective averages selected real loss rows within each sampled unit, applies its detached returned unit weight once, and averages units. `window_mean` and `anchor_transition` retain their backend loss masks; anchor prefixes still supply recurrent context. Priority feedback uses stable unit IDs and the actual loss mask; the backend owns the selected max/mean reducer. Flat losses likewise receive one returned unit weight. Learning sets online train mode and target eval mode. Optimizer success advances the training counter, scheduler and target-copy cadence; an unready opportunity advances none of them. Beta is paced once per actual vector tick, including unscheduled and warmup ticks, before any sample. Sources: [objective, telemetry and update](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:729), [beta pacing](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:643).
+
+X04 telemetry is repaired independently of the optimization objective. Both detached prediction and target operands are promoted to float64 before subtraction; `td_error` is the unweighted mean absolute residual over all sampled real rows, including real anchor-context rows and repeated sampled rows. Padding and IS weights do not alter that denominator. Q telemetry also reduces real predictions in float64. This preserves the existing Python scalar metric and finite true means for the admitted large-residual witness without clipping rewards or changing loss/priority objectives. Source: [float64 producer](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:755).
+
+Production rollout computes full-population Q values. Selection checks that bool eligibility and bool action masks have matching Q-row geometry and device, and refuses an eligible row without a legal action. For K>0 it calls the configured provider once with the K eligible Q/mask/state rows, including aligned epsilons, checks the returned int64[K] shape/device, and scatters the actions into full-N transport. Inactive transport entries retain unmasked argmax. With K=0 it does not call the provider. Recurrent inactive hidden state is preserved. This describes the actual checks: it does not assert independent Q-rank/floating-dtype/self.num_agents/self.action_dim validation or returned-action range/legality validation. Root is separately reconciling the accepted Q4 geometry invariant; narrower documentation neither closes an actual code gap nor weakens that accepted invariant. The checker observes full-N Q/actions and successful actual flat `push_recorded` admission on the currently bound buffer; these recipes use a scripted selector. Genuine-provider selection evidence remains separately attributed. Sources: [rollout and selection](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:998), [scripted eligible callback](/workspace/hamlet/scripts/check_episode_lanes.py:605), [full-N witness](/workspace/hamlet/scripts/check_episode_lanes.py:641), [real-write observer](/workspace/hamlet/scripts/check_episode_lanes.py:725).
+
+## Construction, ownership and preservation boundaries
+
+`VectorizedPopulation.for_training(...)` is the explicit public learner construction seam. It requires all six resolved replay leaves, a nonnegative exact-integer warmup threshold, an explicit NumPy Generator/origin, positive exact-integer vector-tick horizon and its named derivation, and a nonnegative exact-integer current tick, alongside every existing population input. Authored `ReplayBufferConfig.min_size` separately remains positive. One common initializer builds the real selected network/optimizer/replay family; recurrent PER does not require a false non-PER brain or manual buffer attachment. Setup copies the options and Generator. The existing constructor remains callable for construction, inspection and serving without demanding learner-only seed/horizon inputs. Sources: [setup validation](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:112), [factory](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:204), [selected replay construction](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:469).
+
+On actual learning entry, the ordinary constructor lazily resolves the compiled selected level's options/minimum and seed, with explicit population episode limits taking precedence over declared limits. Its recorded beta horizon is their product, an upper bound in vector ticks. The adapter uses a separate PCG64 Generator from the declared training seed where owned sampling is selected; it does not reseed global RNG or borrow curiosity state. The existing successive flat-PER global-sampler role and flat/recurrent uniform RNG roles remain. Per-leaf option provenance remains distinct from the sampler's single origin label. Natural DemoRunner propagation through explicit `for_training` remains T16 work; this draft does not claim that wiring. Sources: [compiled adapter](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:508), [binding](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:595).
+
+Lazy binding distinguishes a genuinely pristine constructor buffer from loaded or externally owned replay. Empty occupancy alone does not authorize replacement, reseeding or loss of archives/IDs/priorities/beta/domains/RNG. Matching qualified current replay is adopted; supported historical/current adaptations build the selected target offside before publication. Ordinary vector ticks cannot rewind. Current sequential7 priority tick must match restored population total_steps; captured6-to-prioritized7 constructs the target at the known restored tick. Sources: [binding checks](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:557), [offside restore](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:2011).
+
+Raw POP6 restore validates current keys, network/optimizer/scheduler/configuration and replay state before installation. The optimizer payload is deep-copied before Torch load so saved input and sibling restores do not share moment/step storage. Replay is materialized once after validation; cumulative counters and current captured history continue. This scoped raw-population behavior does not establish complete native10/7 configuration reconciliation, outer/nested archive accounting, resource/RNG atomicity or full fresh-episode continuation: T24/T25 still own those guarantees. Source: [owned raw restore](/workspace/hamlet/src/townlet/population/vectorized.py:2033).
+
+Approved historical Option A remains: retain old maskless artifacts and original history for archive/query/export, restore compatible available learned state/clocks, and start qualified learning with fresh captured replay. Archive rows neither satisfy warmup nor become optimizer rows through inferred masks. Current captured replay continues; historical adaptation is not permission to discard current qualified rows. Backend archive/serialization details are carried by the [source-verified public API handoff](/workspace/hamlet/.superpowers/sdd/2026-11-01-bac-remediation-upgrades/wave09-preparation/T15-sequence-serialization-api.md:3).
+
+All four architectures, both aggregators, both PER laws, recurrent adapters/objectives/retention/reducers, low-level construction/inspection interfaces, reward components, episode completion/reset/flush and shared-curiosity alternative remain in scope. No capability deletion, consolidation or reduced acceptance is proposed. T15's strict eligible selector evidence does not close private-curiosity runtime isolation/X02. The genuine ICM selector sentinel stops at the second environment boundary before its known reward failure; full transition-context ENV reward/update/continuation remains REQUIRED OPEN under T18e/T18f.
